  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Note: In the given reaction a molecule of $\\mathrm{HCl}$ is lost and $\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{C}$ double bond is formed. Thus it is dehydrohalogenation reaction.\nNitro group is electron withdrawing group. Hence increases the acidity of $\\mathrm{H}$ atom (attached to $\\mathrm{C}$ atom bearing nitro group) which is removed easily. Further the newly formed double bond is in conjugation with nitro group.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0Y-pUsuIdxQlmtM75eNgOgkqe1WY1Rkw5n_LlQt8Bpk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
